A Beginner’s Guide to Uncertainty of Measurement — Bell (@met-bell: 0, is #book, #part-of @met-sources) { r_20P5M8FEB51HDG788TB4YZ90T1
Stephanie Bell. A Beginner’s Guide to Uncertainty of Measurement. National Physical Laboratory, Measurement Good Practice Guide 11, issue 2, 2001. English.

[Publisher’s guide and download](https://www.npl.co.uk/resources/gpgs/beginners-guide-measurement-uncertainty-gpg11) · [Authorized PDF](https://www.npl.co.uk/getattachment/63c00201-a38d-44e5-8470-2440284c3dfe/gpg11_uncertainty.pdf?lang=en-GB).

Read the complete short guide first, including its worked uncertainty calculation, glossary, and cautions. Revisit its explanation of sources, statistical and other evaluations, combining contributions, and reporting as the mathematical material develops. Compare its introductory terminology with the current VIM and JCGM guidance rather than treating a 2001 teaching text as the current complete standard.

Freely available from NPL; retain NPL’s copyright and publication notice. No unrestricted adaptation licence is assumed. The official landing page, author, issue, and downloadable edition were checked on 28 October 2026. The guide remains external to the repository.

